<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila subobscura Turing wavelength at 3.0 µm (Pass 2) — MorphoEval overall 87.8/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 keeps the Schnakenberg field at λ_c = 2.97 µm (3.0 µm detail scale, Holocene, 0 Ma) and closes the Pass 1 gaps. Du at fixed Dv/Du lengthens λ_c monotonically and in proportion to sqrt(Du) (Pearson r = 1 on five values). Setting Dv = Du makes the maximum growth rate -0.233 and the seeded field decays to std 7.7e-9, against a patterned std of 0.100. The 720×480, 12-frame GIF ends on the Cooper 2015 collage with the activator as a 14% pigment modulation inside a border-contrast mask. PDE growth versus the discrete eigenvalue has Pearson r = 0.999998, RMSE = 0.000495, and KS statistic 0.083 (12 modes). Otsu foreground fraction is 0.465 against a border-contrast fraction of 0.771. Wavenumber ratios are 27.80 versus Drosophila simulans and 33.15 versus Drosophila suzukii. The wing-size cline remains a natural-history citation, not a measured 3 µm lattice. Overall 87.8/100 (faithfulness 86.9, reproducibility 90.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit a89be184699d71a03a1673e1f49d8998944a483a; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 90, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_subobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py at a89be184699d71a03a1673e1f49d8998944a483a, image/png, 876428 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 243f026cc7f992905936a2fe98d017a8b769bf166d3d75b449c1ea58fe396813 (sha256 243f026cc7f992905936a2fe98d017a8b769bf166d3d75b449c1ea58fe396813), spec_fingerprint ddf700f45c258daa80240c53b23e60ad30c6cfe8bec1c0e8b9940daf13a758b9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ddf700f45c258daa80240c53b23e60ad30c6cfe8bec1c0e8b9940daf13a758b9; artifact_sha256: 243f026cc7f992905936a2fe98d017a8b769bf166d3d75b449c1ea58fe396813; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_subobscura_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_subobscura_specimen.jpg=5366640b506b5317..., datasets/drosophila_subobscura_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_subobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=0b9b69eda941b675...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Huey et al. (2000) and Gilchrist et al. (2001, 2004) measured latitudinal wing-size clines in introduced D. subobscura. They did not report a pigment wavelength. | Turing (1952) selects a finite critical wavenumber. The Schnakenberg reaction and its use in spatial patterning are from Schnakenberg (1979) and Maini, Painter and Chau (1997).; reconstructed_in_script: k_c for a=0.085, b=1.06, Du=0.041, Dv=0.530, scaled so λ_c = 2.97e-6 m. The nonlinear spot field, the Du sweep, the equal-diffusion ablation, and the specimen-masked render are reconstructions. | Chronospecies contrast uses the predecessor wavelength 8.256e-5 m and the successor wavelength 9.845e-5 m as comparison lengths only. Their kinetics are not copied.; transfer_boundary: A 14% modulation inside the photographic mask makes the GIF resemble the fly because the photograph is in the frame. It does not mean the reaction-diffusion field generated the wing veins, the eye, or the collage layout. | The comparison applies only at this detail scale and age. It does not re-score the 124 µm primordium slot for the same species.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Huey et al. (2000) measured a 3.0 µm Turing wavelength. | Does not claim the spot lattice is a histological section of subobscura pigment granules. | Does not claim nanopublications were signed. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml was present.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.78e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila subobscura Turing wavelength at 3.0 µm (Pass 2) — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Five Du values at fixed Dv/Du give λ_c = 1.451, 1.777, 2.077, 2.406, 2.809. The sequence is strictly increasing and correlates with sqrt(Du) at r = 1. σ(k_c) stays 0.0879, so the sweep changes wavelength rather than merely rescaling time." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

