<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila subobscura Turing wavelength at 3.0 µm (Pass 2) (Drosophila subobscura)",
        "Drosophila subobscura Turing wavelength at 3.0 µm (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Drosophila subobscura morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Drosophila subobscura specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Drosophila subobscura" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Does not claim Huey et al. (2000) measured a 3.0 µm Turing wavelength.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim nanopublications were signed. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml was present.",
        "does_not_claim: Does not claim the spot lattice is a histological section of subobscura pigment granules.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Chronospecies contrast uses the predecessor wavelength 8.256e-5 m and the successor wavelength 9.845e-5 m as comparison lengths only. Their kinetics are not copied.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: k_c for a=0.085, b=1.06, Du=0.041, Dv=0.530, scaled so λ_c = 2.97e-6 m. The nonlinear spot field, the Du sweep, the equal-diffusion ablation, and the specimen-masked render are reconstructions.",
        "reported_in_source: Huey et al. (2000) and Gilchrist et al. (2001, 2004) measured latitudinal wing-size clines in introduced D. subobscura. They did not report a pigment wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) selects a finite critical wavenumber. The Schnakenberg reaction and its use in spatial patterning are from Schnakenberg (1979) and Maini, Painter and Chau (1997).",
        "transfer_boundary: A 14% modulation inside the photographic mask makes the GIF resemble the fly because the photograph is in the frame. It does not mean the reaction-diffusion field generated the wing veins, the eye, or the collage layout.",
        "transfer_boundary: The comparison applies only at this detail scale and age. It does not re-score the 124 µm primordium slot for the same species." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Drosophila subobscura (Palearctic Latitudinal Wing-Size Cline Fly)" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "II. Anaima (Invertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Entoma (Arthropoda)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Drosophila" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-subobscura-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/drosophila_subobscura_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Drosophila subobscura; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Huey et al. (2000) and Gilchrist et al. (2001, 2004) measured latitudinal wing-size clines in introduced D. subobscura. They did not report a pigment wavelength. | Turing (1952) selects a finite critical wavenumber. The Schnakenberg reaction and its use in spatial patterning are from Schnakenberg (1979) and Maini, Painter and Chau (1997).; reconstructed_in_script: k_c for a=0.085, b=1.06, Du=0.041, Dv=0.530, scaled so λ_c = 2.97e-6 m. The nonlinear spot field, the Du sweep, the equal-diffusion ablation, and the specimen-masked render are reconstructions. | Chronospecies contrast uses the predecessor wavelength 8.256e-5 m and the successor wavelength 9.845e-5 m as comparison lengths only. Their kinetics are not copied.; transfer_boundary: A 14% modulation inside the photographic mask makes the GIF resemble the fly because the photograph is in the frame. It does not mean the reaction-diffusion field generated the wing veins, the eye, or the collage layout. | The comparison applies only at this detail scale and age. It does not re-score the 124 µm primordium slot for the same species.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Huey et al. (2000) measured a 3.0 µm Turing wavelength. | Does not claim the spot lattice is a histological section of subobscura pigment granules. | Does not claim nanopublications were signed. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml was present.]; phenomenon_size: 1.9 µm (1.919e-06 m, log10=-5.717 m, tier=3_subcellular_um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 1.9 µm to 4.3 mm): 1.9 µm:drosophila-affinis-bioelectric-polarity, 6.0 µm:drosophila-affinis-vertex-packing, 96 µm:drosophila-affinis-turing-wavelength, 192 µm:drosophila-affinis-clock-wavefront, 432 µm:drosophila-affinis-morphogen-condensation, 528 µm:drosophila-affinis-elastic-buckling, 600 µm:drosophila-affinis-flux-canalization, 840 µm:drosophila-affinis-branching-tree" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-5193(79)90042-0>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1023/a:1013358931816>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1039/a702602a>,
